{"id": "e7e48fdc-7259-4bbc-a6f6-6d14688c20ea", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll check this in two ways. First, I'll look at the current approval status of the model package versions in us-east-1. Second, I'll look at the audit trail to see who or what set each approval, whether a person or an automated role or pipeline.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_WRMSwrXCL4of2ltt1fuJNH", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "sagemaker-approval-check", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["investigating-infrastructure-changes", "discovering-deployments", "searching-logs"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Determine whether model version approvals in the SageMaker Model Registry (us-east-1) are gated by manual human review or are being auto-approved.",
  "context": "User asks if approvals are actually manual or if versions are auto-approved. Agent space account is 012345678901_1 (us-east-1); also check any other associated AWS accounts via list_associations if they have SageMaker model registries. Read-only analysis only; make no changes.",
  "resources": ["SageMaker model package groups and model packages in us-east-1", "CloudTrail events: UpdateModelPackage, CreateModelPackage", "EventBridge rules on 'SageMaker Model Package State Change'", "Lambda functions / SageMaker Pipelines / CodePipeline / CI-CD workflows that call UpdateModelPackage or set ModelApprovalStatus", "Model package group resource policies are out of scope for changes but may be read"],
  "timeframe": "Last 90 days (current time 2026-11-14T04:42:26Z), or as far back as CloudTrail event history permits",
  "criteria": "1) List all model package groups and, per group, counts of versions by ModelApprovalStatus (Approved / PendingManualApproval / Rejected). 2) For Approved versions, determine who/what set approval: check CreateModelPackage requests for ModelApprovalStatus=Approved at creation (e.g. pipeline RegisterModel step with approval_status='Approved') and UpdateModelPackage CloudTrail events (userIdentity type: human IAM user / SSO / assumed-role by person vs service role/Lambda/pipeline/CodeBuild execution roles), plus the time gap between creation and approval (near-instant = likely automated). Check ApprovalDescription and ModelPackage metadata. 3) Look for automation that auto-approves: EventBridge rules, Lambda functions, SageMaker Pipeline definitions (ConditionStep / RegisterModel defaults), CI/CD workflows. 4) Give a clear verdict per group (manual-gated / auto-approved / mixed) with concrete evidence (version numbers, timestamps, principal names) and note any gaps or limitations (e.g. CloudTrail retention). Keep the final report concise."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Check SageMaker Model Registry approval status and approvers in us-east-1"}], "created_at": null}

